00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.710 align:start position:0%
 
we condemn  president putin and the russian  federation  for their unprovoked  illegal  attack and invasion of ukraine  we stand with ukraine we stand with the  people of ukraine  and we stand with canadians here at home  with ties to ukraine  we must use all of the tools available  to us as a country  to defend ukraine in europe against a  vicious authoritarian onslaught  one of the things that canada can do to  support democracies in europe  is for this government to recognize that  canada  is an energy  has immense energy resources  is to recognize that energy is vital to  canadian and european defense and  security  to recognize that natural gas is  consistent with environmental goals in  the transition to non-emitting sources  of energy and to undertake new measures  that ensure natural gas pipelines can be  built and approved to atlantic tidewater  if we can build pipelines to get  canadian natural gas to tidewater we can  displace russian gas in europe  thereby countering the threat from the  russian federation and president  vladimir putin and strengthening  democracy in europe and here at home in  canada  parliament certainly stands to condemn  vladimir putin for their unprovoked  illegal attack and we certainly stand  with the people of ukraine  but what i find  really disturbing and appalling at this  time  is the crass exploitive attitude of the  conservatives to try and take a  humanitarian disaster and use it to  promote the pipe dream of spending  billions of taxpayers dollars on  pipelines they could have talked about  the need for parliament to stand  together to take on russian  disinformation they didn't do that they  could have talked about the food crisis  we're starting to see if we uh see wheat  exports in ukraine cut off they could  have talked about refugees but they're  not interested in that i expect a lot  for many of the conservative  backbenchers but i expect more from this  member  does he not know that quebec has already  shut down lng pipelines so if he's going  to get to tidewater does he not have a  map of canada because quebec says it  will not allow lng exports because it  actually undermines our world  obligations to reduce greenhouse gas  emissions it is clear  it is clear as understood by the  european union that energy is not only  vital to economies it's vital to defense  and security and that's why the  conservatives have introduced this  motion today because it is vital that we  protect the security and defense of this  country and that of our european allies  and partners  let me be clear madam speaker russia's  actions are as deplorable as they are  unacceptable to us and to the  international community  and they indeed may amount to war crimes  under international humanitarian law  which is why we stand together with  other nations referring this to the  international criminal court to  to actually investigate to see whether  war crimes are already being committed  as  my colleague has stated  we will continue to stand with the  ukrainian people and our response has  been strong and it has been  fast  every day we have responded to the  requests of the ukrainian people and the  ukrainian government every day we have  done the things that are meant to  suffocate the russian economy and to  isolate them in the world  madam secret is extremely important that  we continue these important efforts and  not be distracted  not be distracted by other issues we  keep our eye on the ball and ensuring  that we are doing what president  zielinski and the russian government and  the ukrainian government has requested  of us to put that squeeze to suffocate  the russian government this is the way  russians will understand what their  government is doing in their name and  call upon the russian government itself  to stop as well  what  president zielinski has not asked for  is are more pipelines in canada  what president zielinski has not asked  for is a retreat to 20th century energy  policies  what president zielenski has not asked  for is us to engage in a debate this day  about  climate change or about uh oil security  what president zielinski has asked us is  to be laser focused on the problems of  ukraine and to allow  them to have our support on every  critical aspect that they need support  on  i am deeply concerned that the  conservative party doesn't get that  while i absolutely  appreciate their solidarity on our  actions that we have taken  what distresses me greatly is a crass  opportunity that they are taking like an  opportunistic infection  to take advantage of a deeply disturbing  grave international crisis that affects  every one of us in this house every  canadian and everyone would this member  acknowledge that his calling an  infection the the conversation around  energy security which relates to food  security which relates to to poverty  reduction which relates to all of these  very important subjects is misguided and  needed in to ensure that the world has  has peace and security both in ukraine  going forward and  i have to allow for other questions i'm  going to give the benefit of the doubt  here to members from all other political  parties that have seemed to think that  this is somehow about a a a big oil  vendetta well mountain speaker the  reality is is that uh the the the energy  security situation in europe is has been  funding the war in the ukraine and now  it is a high time for us to acknowledge  the fact that we need to ensure that  there are ethical sources of energy that  that that do not go into the hands of  despots but specifically will this  member acknowledge that it's not simply  oiling oil it is the the the ingredients  that are required for things like  fertilizer which with a upcoming growing  season in the ukraine madam speaker will  be absolutely essential for ensuring  that the people of ukraine cannot just  have energy security but long-term food  security as well  the cynicism  the exploitation  of the using a humanitarian disaster to  promote once again the interests of the  oil sector  i'm actually appalled i know that  there's many on the conservative back  bench who would take that position  without even blinking but i've always  had great respect for the member for  wellington halton hills not to play such  a stunt at this time in our history  because this motion could have talked  about the need to deal with russian  disinformation  and a strong position by our parliament  we would have supported that  we could have talked about the need to  help  in visas and the refugee crisis  is clogging the polish border and all of  us could have stood together as a  parliament and supported that  we could have talked about the growing  food crisis that we're facing as  ukrainian is one of the world's bread  baskets and the crisis of that war and  what it means for global food supplies  but the conservatives aren't interested  in that  because the conservatives  fundamental view of the world has always  been to take as much public money and  blow it on oil and gas even though oil  and gas is making enormous profits but  they want the public to pay for it so  now what they've decided is when there's  a humanitarian crisis  well that's another good reason  for them  to shamelessly  promote something like this  i'm actually embarrassed madame speaker  that as the world is looking for  solidarity and a vision of democracy and  freedom and rights that we're here  having to play games  of promoting the interests  of oil and gas once again in a petrol  state like canada

